  "reason": "S478 (s478-boot-match-element): W-ENGINE-MATCH-IN-STATE-CHILD is a CARRIED impl#1 divergence, not the language rule — its §34 row: \"(Carried impl#1 divergence — NOT the language rule. The language SUPPORTS a block `<match>` in a state-child, §51.0.B / §18.0.1, S439 ruling #5 …)\" and it names impl#1's innerHTML re-entry defect. §18.0.1: \"A block `<match>` MAY appear inside the body of a DISPATCHED arm — a block-form `<match>` arm, or an `<engine>` state-child (§51.0.B) — and SHALL NOT be refused there.\" The bootstrap lowers a state-child body as a Cond arm whose `<match>` is rebuilt on every entry (lower.scrml stateView / matchView), so it has no divergence to warn about. The twin keeps the case's runtime half (the page-load render) and asserts the warning does not fire."
